nfused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838127664","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115766#issuecomment-3838127664","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115766","id":3838127664,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kxS4w","user":{"login":"kaluluosi","id":1620585,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjA1ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1620585?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi","html_url":"https://github.com/kaluluosi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kaluluosi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T00:52:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T01:05:44Z","body":"> Check the SDFGI debug draw modes in the **Perspective** menu (**Display Advanced > SDFGI Albedo**). This will let you see whether walls are thick enough to fill in the SDF representation (if not, light is expected to leak through).\n> \n> > This light leakage issue also affects volumetric fog, causing a layer of fog to appear on thick walls when the volumetric fog energy is turned up.\n> \n> Try decreasing **Volumetric Fog > GI Inject** to `0.0` in the Environment resource and see if it's still there.\n\n>  walls are thick enough to fill...\n\nWhat 3D engine requires a 3-meter-thick wall to block light without leakage? Moreover, actual tests have shown that there is no necessary relationship with the thickness of the wall. As long as the mesh of the bounding box is not a single closed one, even if you use a 1-kilometer-thick wall to piece together a box, DirectLight3D will still leak light.\n\nYou must use a Cube Mesh, and the wall must be at least 3 meters away from the indoor scene to completely block the light of DirectLight3D.\n\nIf SDFGI is not enabled, even a piece of paper can block DirectLight3D.\n\n\nMy Environment settings: I only turned on SDFGI and didn't use VoxelGI.\n\n<img width=\"302\" height=\"883\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4093d41e-4b24-46e3-b546-bf784b5f7884\" />\n\n## SDFGI Cascades\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1040\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e61b49b5-363e-4a67-9ca3-17289699563e\" />\n\n## SDFGI Probes\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1040\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2943070b-ed65-4a64-aec0-709820e3fadd\" />\n\n<img width=\"1572\" height=\"694\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a52c4ca6-254f-4bc8-a71c-3e239f03507b\" />\n\n<img width=\"1139\" height=\"550\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/214ae852-e756-49ed-ac94-1fd19de9dd2d\" />\n\n## SDFGI Buffer\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1040\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa3fbd79-0dd3-4c09-a8f6-593ffc2a6970\" />\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1040\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9d8fc259-d73a-46ee-962b-78d1a38834f6\" />\n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838127664/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]